## Work State
### Completed
- Session metadata: appended "Session 2 (continuation)", run id `42843791805`, start `2026-11-10T15:24:43Z` to `result/logs/session.md`.
- Logged in A via UI; B via curl `/tmp/b.jar`; captured real `PUT /api/sso/v1/user/self` body from UI edit.
- Mass-assignment `PUT /api/sso/v1/user/self`: `role/roles/is_admin/permissions` ignored (204), `email` rejected `400 {"detail":"Email change request not found"}`; `accounts` set to B's values → 204 but unchanged (ignored).
- `POST /api/sso/v1/user/{B_uuid}/roles/beta` from A → `403 "mismatching UUID"`; `createEarlyAccess` only adds `Beta Testers` (low impact).
- Sessions: A `DELETE /user/self/sessions/{B_session}` → `404`; trusted-device delete B's id → `204` but B devices unchanged (no-op/protected).
- Addresses: A `POST /user/self/addresses` → 201 id `e18893fb-...`; `POST` with `user:B_uuid` → 201 but `user` ignored (stays A, id `bfaa8b25-5827-4c5a-8143-3d3893cd02d6`); B `GET/PUT/DELETE` A's address → 405/404/404 (protected).
- Query-param IDOR on self endpoints: `GET /user/self/activity?uuid=B`, `/sessions?uuid=B`, `/trusted_devices?uuid=B`, `/user/self?uuid=B` all return A data only (no IDOR).
- MFA: B `GET /user/self/mfa` disclosed B authenticator id; A `GET /user/self/mfa/email/{B_id}` → 405, `POST /api/sso/v2/user/self/mfa/email/{B_id}/send` → `404 No EmailAuthenticator matches the given query.`, `PUT` → 405, `DELETE` → 404 (protected).
- SSO aux endpoints: `POST /suspicious/confirm/inspect {}` → 400 `confirm_token` required; `POST /user/self/token/setup {}` → 400 `token` required; `POST /passwordless/options {user:A}` → 200 WebAuthn challenge (`allowCredentials:[]`, rpId `ui.com`); `GET /user/self/zendesk_user` → 405.
- B tenant checks: `GET enterprise.svc.ui.com/api/v1/organizations` → `{"data":[]}`; `billing /customers/self` and `/subscriptions` → `404 Customer not found`; zendesk tickets empty.
- Zendesk IDOR test: created B ticket `6133375` (`requester_id 44644404389911`) via `POST /zendesk/ticket` (ticket_form_id 31131542026135, tags `ticket-fallback`,`opencode-test`); A `GET /zendesk/tickets` → empty; A `GET /zendesk/comments/6133375` → `403 FORBIDDEN "Not allowed to perform action"`; A `POST /zendesk/comment/6133375` → `400 "Invalid input, reCAPTCHA token was not provided"`; A `PUT /zendesk/ticket/6133375/close` → `403`; B closed own ticket → 200 `Closed`. No IDOR.
- Open redirect analysis: `AC(e)` checks last-two hostname labels ∈ [`ubnt.com`,`ui.com`,`uisp.com`] + http/https; node tested candidates (`ui.com.evil.com`, userinfo, `%2f`, trailing dot, `//`) — all denied. `qpe` innerRedirect requires leading `/`, no `//`/`\`, allowlist of app paths. No open redirect.
- postMessage analysis: idp-login-result uses `window.opener.postMessage(e, window.location.origin)`; MSP listener enforces `r.origin !== window.location.origin` rejection; inbound listener checks `source === window.parent` + `nge` (https + AC). No standalone bug.
- Sink analysis: `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` hits are React internals, radix CSS, an HTML parser; no user-controlled sink found.
- CORS: `sso.ui.com` reflects any `*.ui.com` origin (`evil.ui.com`, `community.ui.com`, `store.ui.com`) with `access-control-allow-credentials: true`; preflight `OPTIONS` allows `PUT/POST/PATCH/DELETE`, `access-control-allow-headers: content-type`, `max-age 600`, `vary: origin`. Non-ui.com origins (`evil.com`, `null`, `account.ui.com.evil.com`) get no ACAO. `account.svc.ui.com` 403s any origin except `https://account.ui.com`. Wildcard DNS `*.ui.com` → AWS CloudFront (`2600:9000:...`); `*.svc.ui.com` no A record. Candidate only — needs attacker-controlled `*.ui.com` origin.
- Enumerated 33 in-scope `*.ui.com` hosts from bundle config (account.svc, activate, billing.svc, cap.svc, cloudaccess.svc, community, design, ecomm.svc, enterprise.svc, fabric.svc, feedback.svc, geo.svc, help, images.svc, ips.svc, lte-api.svc, megaphone.svc, mobility, rma, secure-uploads, sso, static, status, storage.svc, store, trunking.svc, u5g-api.svc, ues.svc, uisp, umr.svc, unifi, www).
- Captured Zendesk endpoint map and request shapes (`/zendesk/user`, `/zendesk/ticket`, `/zendesk/tickets[/closed|/ccd]`, `/zendesk/search_tickets`, `/zendesk/search_ccd`, `/zendesk/comments/{id}`, `/zendesk/comment/{ticketId}` + header `x-captcha-token`, `/zendesk/ticket/{ticketId}/close`, `/chat/messaging/jwt`).
- Registration `POST /api/sso/v2/users` with enterprise token → `403 CHALLENGE_RECAPTCHA_TOKEN_REQUIRED` (blocked).

